1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
If you give a mouse a cookie,

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,980
then it'll ask for a glass of milk.

3
00:00:09,983 --> 00:00:11,983
Then one thing will lead to another

4
00:00:11,983 --> 00:00:13,983
And you never know what's next

5
00:00:13,983 --> 00:00:15,983
Let's go to unexpected places

6
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:17,983
They'll leave us smiling faces

7
00:00:17,983 --> 00:00:19,963
With loose big cat and dog

8
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:21,527
So come on, come along

9
00:00:21,527 --> 00:00:23,407
If you gave a mouse a cookie

10
00:00:23,407 --> 00:00:25,307
You'll never know what you get

11
00:00:25,307 --> 00:00:27,247
If you gave a mouse a cookie

12
00:00:27,247 --> 00:00:29,767
What do you think will happen next?

13
00:00:29,951 --> 00:00:39,931
*music*

14
00:00:39,935 --> 00:00:43,775
- Oliver, time to get up.

15
00:00:43,775 --> 00:00:44,935
- Okay, Mom.

16
00:00:47,935 --> 00:00:49,915
A mouse?

17
00:00:49,919 --> 00:00:51,119
Can I have a crayon?

18
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:52,459
A crayon?

19
00:00:52,559 --> 00:00:53,859
Um, sure.

20
00:00:56,019 --> 00:00:57,019
Thanks!

21
00:00:57,119 --> 00:00:59,899
Woo-hoo-hoo!

22
00:00:59,903 --> 00:01:03,603
If you give a mouse a crayon, then...

23
00:01:03,603 --> 00:01:09,883
Mouse, what do you want it for?

24
00:01:09,887 --> 00:01:13,587
I want to draw my own comic book.

25
00:01:13,587 --> 00:01:15,427
None of these have mice.

26
00:01:15,427 --> 00:01:19,867
My comic is about an evil scientist named Dr. Crabby.

27
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:22,211
One day, Dr. Crabby went to work in his laboratory,

28
00:01:22,331 --> 00:01:24,251
and when he came out, he laughed and said,

29
00:01:24,371 --> 00:01:27,871
"He he he he he, and now for my greatest invention,

30
00:01:28,011 --> 00:01:29,851
the Toy Trapper XK-10,000."

31
00:01:29,855 --> 00:01:32,355
What do you think of my comic book so far?

32
00:01:32,355 --> 00:01:33,355
It's great!

33
00:01:33,355 --> 00:01:37,355
But what's Dr. Crabby going to do with the Toy Trapper XK-10,000?

34
00:01:37,355 --> 00:01:39,835
He wants to take all the toys to the toy.

35
00:01:39,839 --> 00:01:41,839
in the entire universe for himself.

36
00:01:41,839 --> 00:01:43,839
Nobody else can have any toys.

37
00:01:43,839 --> 00:01:45,839
- Yikes, that is mean.

38
00:01:45,839 --> 00:01:49,819
- Yeah, but don't worry, Oliver.

39
00:01:49,823 --> 00:01:54,823
Because the masked mouse is about to come to the rescue!

40
00:01:54,903 --> 00:01:57,823
The masked mouse destroys the Toy Trapper XK-10,000

41
00:01:57,903 --> 00:01:59,803
and everyone gets their toys now.

42
00:01:59,807 --> 00:02:02,347
Hooray for the Masked Mouse!

43
00:02:02,347 --> 00:02:04,347
Do you have a superhero motto?

44
00:02:04,347 --> 00:02:06,847
Um... Hmm...

45
00:02:06,847 --> 00:02:09,787
The Masked Mouse is a vampire.

46
00:02:09,791 --> 00:02:13,291
a friend indeed to anyone in need.

47
00:02:13,291 --> 00:02:14,371
- I like it.

48
00:02:14,371 --> 00:02:17,471
- Thanks, and now I know just what I need.

49
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:19,771
- If a mouse draws a picture of himself as a superman,

50
00:02:19,775 --> 00:02:21,775
Then...

51
00:02:24,775 --> 00:02:29,755
Ooh! A cape!

52
00:02:29,759 --> 00:02:32,599
And my own superhero logo!

53
00:02:35,599 --> 00:02:36,599
What?

54
00:02:36,699 --> 00:02:39,739
He's going to want to be a superhero again.

55
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:41,583
in real life, too.

56
00:02:42,703 --> 00:02:46,543
The masked mouse, ready for it all!

57
00:02:46,643 --> 00:02:49,723
Oh, mouse!

58
00:02:49,727 --> 00:02:52,727
I'm okay. I guess being a superhero takes practice.

59
00:02:52,727 --> 00:02:55,227
Oliver, time to go to the store.

60
00:02:55,227 --> 00:02:59,707
When mom says it's time to go, then it's time to go.

61
00:02:59,711 --> 00:03:01,051
What are you going to the store for?

62
00:03:01,051 --> 00:03:03,171
New sneakers for Pee Wee Softball.

63
00:03:03,171 --> 00:03:06,671
Uh-oh, I guess we left kind of a mess.

64
00:03:06,671 --> 00:03:08,171
I should clean that up.

65
00:03:08,171 --> 00:03:09,691
Stand back, Oliver.

66
00:03:09,695 --> 00:03:13,195
This is a job for the masked mouse.

67
00:03:14,535 --> 00:03:16,735
Really? You don't mind cleaning up?

68
00:03:16,835 --> 00:03:19,675
Helping others is a superhero's number one job.

69
00:03:19,679 --> 00:03:21,679
Thanks, Mouse. Be back soon.

70
00:03:21,679 --> 00:03:25,639
Time for the masked mouse to spring into action!

71
00:03:29,663 --> 00:03:31,663
Ha!

72
00:03:31,663 --> 00:03:32,663
Ha!

73
00:03:38,663 --> 00:03:39,643
Yes!

74
00:03:39,647 --> 00:03:41,647
Whoa!

75
00:03:45,147 --> 00:03:46,147
Uh-oh.

76
00:03:46,687 --> 00:03:48,487
Oh, I know just what I need.

77
00:03:48,487 --> 00:03:49,627
The vacuum cleaner.

78
00:03:49,631 --> 00:03:50,631
Come on.

79
00:03:50,631 --> 00:03:51,631
Oh dear.

80
00:03:54,631 --> 00:03:55,631
Come on.

81
00:03:55,631 --> 00:03:56,631
Come on.

82
00:03:56,631 --> 00:03:57,631
Come on.

83
00:03:57,631 --> 00:03:58,631
Come on.

84
00:03:58,631 --> 00:03:59,631
Oh dear.

85
00:03:59,615 --> 00:04:01,615
Oh my, my groceries!

86
00:04:01,615 --> 00:04:02,615
Hark!

87
00:04:02,615 --> 00:04:04,615
Looks like Moose is in trouble.

88
00:04:04,615 --> 00:04:06,615
And if someone is in trouble,

89
00:04:06,615 --> 00:04:09,595
then the masked mouse has to help.

90
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:10,599
Whoa!

91
00:04:16,899 --> 00:04:19,579
Don't worry, Moose. I'll save you.

92
00:04:19,583 --> 00:04:24,583
- Oh, my oranges! - No problem for the masked mouse.

93
00:04:24,583 --> 00:04:29,563
- -

94
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:31,567
Oh!

95
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:39,547
Pardon me, Piper. May I borrow your net?

96
00:04:39,551 --> 00:04:42,391
Why, certainly, mysterious masked mouse.

97
00:04:47,391 --> 00:04:49,531
Coming through!

98
00:04:49,535 --> 00:04:51,535
Whoa!

99
00:04:51,535 --> 00:04:52,535
Whoa!

100
00:04:52,535 --> 00:04:55,535
Whee! Whoa!

101
00:04:57,535 --> 00:04:59,515
Whoa!

102
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:01,819
Oh no, I can't look.

103
00:05:03,279 --> 00:05:04,119
Got it!

104
