107
00:05:14,003 --> 00:05:16,003
I just have to go through 'em.

108
00:05:18,003 --> 00:05:19,483
Woo!

109
00:05:19,487 --> 00:05:22,987
And then save the last orange.

110
00:05:22,987 --> 00:05:26,867
Why, thank you, Masked Mouse.

111
00:05:26,867 --> 00:05:29,467
All in a day's work.

112
00:05:29,471 --> 00:05:31,471
Is that a cry for help?

113
00:05:31,471 --> 00:05:33,471
Because if that's a cry for help,

114
00:05:33,471 --> 00:05:36,471
then Masked Mouse must ride to the rescue.

115
00:05:36,471 --> 00:05:38,471
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

116
00:05:38,471 --> 00:05:39,451
Come back!

117
00:05:39,455 --> 00:05:41,115
- Yeah, come back here.

118
00:05:41,115 --> 00:05:41,955
- No.

119
00:05:46,955 --> 00:05:49,435
- Masked mouse to the right.

120
00:05:49,439 --> 00:05:50,739
How can I help?

121
00:05:50,739 --> 00:05:51,739
- Dog's boat.

122
00:05:51,739 --> 00:05:52,579
- My boat.

123
00:05:52,579 --> 00:05:53,419
- He lost it.

124
00:05:53,419 --> 00:05:54,579
- I lost it.

125
00:05:54,579 --> 00:05:56,039
It's gone into the middle of the fountain

126
00:05:56,039 --> 00:05:59,419
and I can't get it back and I want it.

127
00:05:59,423 --> 00:06:02,423
I really, really, really want it.

128
00:06:02,423 --> 00:06:04,423
Don't worry, I'll save your boat.

129
00:06:04,423 --> 00:06:08,423
If Dog's boat is trapped in the middle of the fountain, then...

130
00:06:08,423 --> 00:06:09,403
Aha!

131
00:06:09,407 --> 00:06:12,407
I, the masked mouse, will make a new one.

132
00:06:16,407 --> 00:06:19,387
He is gonna make a boat out of that recycle.

133
00:06:19,391 --> 00:06:20,391
How's she gonna do that?

134
00:06:20,391 --> 00:06:21,391
Yeah, how?

135
00:06:25,391 --> 00:06:26,391
Ta-da!

136
00:06:27,391 --> 00:06:28,391
Nyeh!

137
00:06:28,391 --> 00:06:29,371
Nyeh!

138
00:06:29,375 --> 00:06:32,875
Wow, that is the coolest thing ever.

139
00:06:32,875 --> 00:06:34,875
Totally the coolest.

140
00:06:37,875 --> 00:06:39,355
Excuse me, sir.

141
00:06:39,359 --> 00:06:41,359
What are you doing with that popsicle stick?

142
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:43,359
Uh, throwing it away?

143
00:06:43,359 --> 00:06:45,359
No need. I'll take that.

144
00:06:46,359 --> 00:06:47,359
Whoa!

145
00:06:47,359 --> 00:06:49,359
Yay!

146
00:06:49,343 --> 00:06:58,143
Oh, thank you, thank you, thank you, thank you, thank you!

147
00:06:59,327 --> 00:07:04,327
Oh, look, Oliver and Mom are getting on the bus and heading home.

148
00:07:04,327 --> 00:07:09,307
I still didn't clean up the crayon mess like I said I would.

149
00:07:09,311 --> 00:07:12,311
And a superhero always keeps his word.

150
00:07:12,311 --> 00:07:14,691
Only, Oliver is on a bus,

151
00:07:14,691 --> 00:07:17,691
and a bus is faster than a mini mouse-sized skateboard.

152
00:07:17,691 --> 00:07:19,291
I'll never make it home in time.

153
00:07:19,295 --> 00:07:20,455
Time to clean it up.

154
00:07:20,455 --> 00:07:24,435
La, la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la.

155
00:07:24,435 --> 00:07:25,835
Unless...

156
00:07:27,535 --> 00:07:28,295
Hi, Pig.

157
00:07:28,295 --> 00:07:29,275
Can you give me a ride?

158
00:07:29,279 --> 00:07:30,739
I left a bit of a mess at home,

159
00:07:30,739 --> 00:07:32,579
and I need to get back quickly to clean it up.

160
00:07:32,579 --> 00:07:35,159
Unfortunately, I can't go anywhere right now.

161
00:07:35,159 --> 00:07:36,159
Why not?

162
00:07:36,159 --> 00:07:38,279
Because my scooter isn't working.

163
00:07:38,279 --> 00:07:39,259
Um...

164
00:07:39,263 --> 00:07:41,423
seems to be working perfectly fine to me.

165
00:07:41,423 --> 00:07:43,103
Something is wrong with my radio.

166
00:07:45,863 --> 00:07:48,143
You can't ride a scooter without a radio.

167
00:07:48,143 --> 00:07:49,243
It simply isn't.

168
00:07:49,247 --> 00:07:52,747
Whenever I am scootering, I like to listen to jaunty tunes.

169
00:07:52,747 --> 00:07:56,387
Without them, a scooter ride is just eh.

170
00:07:56,387 --> 00:07:59,227
- -

171
00:07:59,231 --> 00:08:01,231
It's hopeless.

172
00:08:01,231 --> 00:08:03,231
Oh, no, it isn't.

173
00:08:03,231 --> 00:08:04,231
Huh?

174
00:08:04,231 --> 00:08:08,231
Not when the masked mouse is here to save you.

175
00:08:08,231 --> 00:08:09,211
Hm.

176
00:08:09,215 --> 00:08:10,715
I see.

177
00:08:10,815 --> 00:08:11,515
Got it!

178
00:08:11,615 --> 00:08:12,315
Try it now!

179
00:08:15,515 --> 00:08:17,715
Why, thank you, Masked Mouse!

180
00:08:17,815 --> 00:08:19,195
All in a day's work.

181
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,999
There were pancake crumbs in your wiring.

182
00:08:21,099 --> 00:08:22,399
I see.

183
00:08:22,499 --> 00:08:24,799
Well, let that be a lesson to us all.

184
00:08:24,899 --> 00:08:27,799
Never snack and drive.

185
00:08:27,899 --> 00:08:29,179
Now, let's go.

186
00:08:29,183 --> 00:08:30,183
